From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:14:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath9k: let the page_pool recycle directly from NAPI

Tie the RX page_pool to the NAPI instance. Pages freed in that NAPI's
softirq context, which covers frames the stack consumes or drops while
the poll runs, then go straight back into the pool's lockless cache
instead of through its ptr_ring.

The pool must not outlive this link with NAPI still enabled:
ath9k_deinit_device() and the error path of ath9k_init_device() already
disable NAPI before ath_rx_cleanup() destroys the pool, and the pool is
created after netif_napi_add() while NAPI is still disabled.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c
index c060e3a..c69ed94 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c
@@ -133,6 +133,7 @@ static int ath_rx_page_pool_create(struct ath_softc *sc, int nbufs)
 	pp_params.pool_size = DIV_ROUND_UP(nbufs, (PAGE_SIZE << order) / size);
 	pp_params.nid = NUMA_NO_NODE;
 	pp_params.dev = sc->dev;
+	pp_params.napi = &sc->napi;
 	pp_params.flags = PP_FLAG_DMA_MAP;
 
 	/* EDMA chips clear the RX status from the CPU side */
